    <item>
      <title>Many people I'm talking to are getting very frustrated with this market. My feel</title>
      <link>https://t.me/barchartx/1993</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;Many people I'm talking to are getting very frustrated with this market. My&lt;br/&gt;feeling is it's because of two main factors:&lt;br/&gt;1) Not accepting that the market is in a corrective phase. The Nasdaq Composite&lt;br/&gt;is below its 200-day moving average and there's too much complacency in my view.&lt;br/&gt;Sentiment is not washed out yet.&lt;br/&gt;2) They are not cutting losses on stocks down 20-50% (or more) off their highs.&lt;br/&gt;Mainly because they are married to the huge winners of the past and do not want&lt;br/&gt;to let go of them (nor I am saying to sell them because this is not investment&lt;br/&gt;advice).&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This is mainly for people who like to actively manage their accounts and who&lt;br/&gt;like to trade growth stocks. It's going to take some time for conditions to be&lt;br/&gt;healthy again. Just be patient. In the meantime, protect your capital, protect&lt;br/&gt;your confidence, and as always, know your timeframe. Good luck!&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;@​jfahmy • Nov 16, 2026&lt;/div&gt;</description>
